  <div style="background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.75); border: 1.5px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08); border-radius: 14px; padding: 24px 20px; box-shadow: 0 10px 25px rgba(0,0,0,0.35); transition: transform 0.2s ease, border-color 0.2s ease;">
    <div style="display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; width: 42px; height: 42px; border-radius: 10px; background: #3b82f622; color: #3b82f6; font-weight: 800; font-size: 1.05rem; margin-bottom: 14px;">03</div>
    <h3 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.1rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 10px; line-height: 1.4;">Valid Insurance Certificate</h3>
    <p style="color: #94a3b8; font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.65; margin: 0;">The insurer’s policy must cover the cargo for the entire journey, including loading, unloading, and transit. The certificate should list the insured value, the policy number, and the coverage period.</p>
  </div>
  <div style="background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.75); border: 1.5px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08); border-radius: 14px; padding: 24px 20px; box-shadow: 0 10px 25px rgba(0,0,0,0.35); transition: transform 0.2s ease, border-color 0.2s ease;">
    <div style="display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; width: 42px; height: 42px; border-radius: 10px; background: #a855f722; color: #a855f7; font-weight: 800; font-size: 1.05rem; margin-bottom: 14px;">04</div>
    <h3 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.1rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 10px; line-height: 1.4;">IBA‑Approved Consignment Bilty</h3>
    <p style="color: #94a3b8; font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.65; margin: 0;">The Indian Baggage Association (IBA) consignment bilty serves as the primary transport document. It records the cargo details, consignor and consignee information, and the agreed freight charges. The bilty must be signed by both parties and retained by the carrier.</p>
  </div>
</div>

<p>While the above documents are mandatory, the most critical safeguard for high‑value goods is the <strong>100% Declared‑Value Marine Transit Insurance</strong>. This type of coverage ensures that the entire declared value of the shipment is protected against loss, theft, or damage during transit, regardless of the cause.</p>
<p>Unlike standard liability policies that cap payouts at a fixed sum, a declared‑value policy ties the indemnity directly to the actual worth of the goods. For clients transporting electronics, jewelry, or other high‑risk items, this insurance is not just advisable – it’s a financial necessity.</p>

<p>In summary, a compliant move from Coimbatore to Bangalore hinges on these four key documents, with the 100% declared‑value marine transit insurance standing out as the ultimate safety net for your cargo. Always verify that each paper is current, accurately attested, and retained in both electronic and hard‑copy formats for audit purposes.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>


<section class="content-ui-section" style="padding: 55px 0; background: #0b132b; color: #cbd5e1; border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.07);">
  <div class="container" style="max-width: 1060px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 0 15px;">
    <div style="background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.65); border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08); border-radius: 16px; padding: 36px 32px; box-shadow: 0 12px 30px rgba(0,0,0,0.35);">
      <span style="background: rgba(245, 158, 11, 0.12); color: #f59e0b; border: 1px solid rgba(245, 158, 11, 0.35); padding: 4px 14px; border-radius: 20px; font-size: 0.78rem; font-weight: 700; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.5px; display: inline-block; margin-bottom: 14px;">HANDOVER INSPECTION</span>
      <h2 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.7rem; font-weight: 800; line-height: 1.35; margin-bottom: 18px;">Destination Handover, Odometer Sign-Off &amp; Joint Condition Inspection for packers and movers coimbatore to bangalore</h2>
      <div style="font-size: 1.02rem; line-height: 1.8; color: #cbd5e1;"><p>At the destination, the delivery handover for each two‑wheeler or motorcycle follows a strict protocol that guarantees transparency and accountability for both the carrier and the customer. The first step is a daylight re‑inspection of the vehicle’s exterior and interior against the original pickup photographs taken by the driver.</p>
<p>This visual audit confirms that no new scratches, dents, or fluid leaks have appeared during transit. The inspector uses a standardized checklist to capture any deviations, photographing the vehicle from multiple angles and tagging each image with the vehicle’s registration number and the delivery timestamp.</p>

<p>Next, the odometer reading is verified against the original logbook (LR bilty) that recorded the mileage at pickup. The carrier reads the current mileage, compares it with the bilty entry, and notes any discrepancy.</p>
<p>If the mileage difference exceeds the pre‑agreed tolerance level, a written note is added to the delivery report and the customer is notified immediately. This step ensures that the vehicle has not been subjected to unauthorized mileage manipulation or excessive wear.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>



